From c322ead2444d0e4d2d2fe15691a70de60dc91cb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Calogero Mandracchia <calogero@efebia.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:49:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] channels: hold channel input behind a per-thread barrier

A host can close a thread's channel barrier before it captures the
thread. While it is closed, no channel input reaches the model: input
that reaches the thread is held in order with a sequence number, and
input a turn did not record is held instead of discarded. Closing asks
the servers to stop accepting input; each answers with a marker after
the input it accepted before, which is never shown to the model.

A snapshot reports the held and in-flight input, the servers' connection
and fence state, what still blocks the drain and what may have been
lost. The host releases held input it kept elsewhere, up to a sequence
number, or opens the barrier, which drops the held input it discards
and delivers the rest.
